      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Fractional output comparison\n\nModels: `kandinsky_imagesr_2.0.safetensors` (huggingface.co/hmdlsk/Kandinsky-ImageSR-2.0-ComfyUI) in `ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/` and the FLUX.1 VAE `ae.safetensors` in `ComfyUI/models/vae/`.\n\n**native restoration scale** (`upscale_factor`, 2x or 4x) is the scale the model actually restores at: it sets the tile geometry, the cost and the meaning of creativity. **output_scale** only sets the final size: the finished restoration is resized with antialiased bicubic resampling to round(input size x output_scale). 0 keeps the native size; 1.0 restores without enlarging. Restoring at 2x and outputting 1.2x costs the same as a plain 2x restoration.\n\nThe transformer runs once (native 2x, creativity 1). The reduced versions are made from that single result with ComfyUI's built-in Upscale Image By node (Lanczos) so that no restoration is repeated; they are close to, but not bit-identical with, what output_scale produces (see workflow 06), and the built-in node may round a dimension differently at exact halves. The bicubic baseline enlarges the original without restoration. Files are saved under `kandinsky_sr/cmp_*` with the restoration scale, output scale and creativity in the name."
      ],
      "title": "Kandinsky ImageSR",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
